 that I wanted to fly I wanted that  experience  miramar served as the inspiration for  the movie Top Gun which in turn became  inspiration for cardona's dad Joey this  is Ghost Rider requesting a flyby every  time I ask for something I was a little  bit out of the ordinary my dad would  give me the old that's a negative  ghostrider the pattern is full I wasn't  trying to buzz at our anything with that  but he'd always give me that line as if  Hollywood scripted it Cardona was able  to combine his two passions when it came  time for college he'd filled out and  grown enough to be recruited by the u.s.  Naval Academy to play football while his  sixth resize would keep Cardona from the  cockpit it became his advantage as a  long snapper for your starter for the  Midshipmen the length of my torso  essentially disqualified me from flying  in every platform that I wanted to you  know and that's when I really had to  take a take a moment and reassess what I  wanted to do and so I had to give up my  dream of flying jets and you know being  maverick cookies in 2015 Cardona became  just the fourth long snapper ever  drafted in the NFL but there was still  the issue of his military service which  at the time meant active duty for all  service Academy graduates there was a  point where I didn't know whether or not  I'd actually be able to play in the NFL  or whether I'd have to you know go  active duty and and be in that role that  I'd prepared for Cardona would spend his  rookie season fulfilling his service  obligations 60 miles away from the  Patriots home in Newport Rhode Island  working for the Navy at night and one  full day a week at the Naval Academy of  preparatory school I'd to spend my leave  to go to training camp and being a  rookie an NFL is hard enough but I was  also trying to find my bearings as a  junior officer fortunately you know if  you do your job on the military side and  you're taking care of everything you  need to with your command you know we  don't care what you do with your free  time go ahead play football for this  yeah exactly  your full-time job is being in the Navy  but your full-time job is a rookie with  the New England Patriots does that sound  at all crazy to you  it absolutely sounds crazy to me even  looking back  I can't even imagine doing that again I  think I was so ingrained with with those  core values of the Naval Academy you  know it's like honor courage and  commitment you know and having to uphold  those his dedication hasn't been lost on  his teammates including kicker Stephen  Gostkowski we play 16 games and we're  here all day every day and talk about  football and work out for football and  do training for football and you know he  would come in and practice enough to go  work another job and put things into  perspective after two Super Bowl titles  and a switch from active to reserve duty  Cardona remains as steadfast in his  commitment to both the military and the  NFL in June his military promotion  ceremony was held on the same day as the  Patriots got their new Super Bowl rings  there was just a really special thing  there to see you know guys like Brady  and Edelman go up to them and hug them  and tell them thank you for your service  when you look at where you are right now  early in your NFL career early in your  military career how long can you keep  doing both that is a great question I  don't know how long but I'm going to  continue to do the best I can as long as  they you know let me fulfill either role  you know Cardona talks about this idea  the ideals behind both the military and  the Patriots and those ideals that are  instilled in him and it was both  organizations really having some  flexibility to allow him to do this as  well I have just one question isn't he  tired he seemed as he thought back about  it how tired he was now with the  reserves obviously it frees up more time  for him but there other guys who are  doing this right now the Vikings also  have a long snapper who came out of the  Air Force the army on the Eagles squad  the Steelers have someone there about a  handful of guys right now from service  academies that are playing he might be  tired but it's working for him yeah  there's no time to get into trouble  there's no time to focus on anything  else

